# a whole number with a vulgar fraction glued after it is the mixed number (decision mixed-number-glyph)
'3½'	3.5
'2¾'	2.75
'-1¼'	-1.25
'3½ * 2'	7
# a decimal before the fraction names no mixed number: refused at its place
'2.5½'	error	a mixed number is whole before its fraction
# a fraction alone stays itself; digits glued after it multiply it
'½'	0.5
'½3'	1.5
